vim: set filetype=nroff:




[EXIT STATUS]
Mdview exits 0 on success, and non-zero otherwise.




[EXAMPLES]
.TP
Start the graphical Viewer displaying the help page. Press [F1] for more help.
.B mdview
.TP
View help in the console.
.B mdview \-\-help
.sp 0
.B mdview \-\-bare \-h
.TP
View the README file located in the current directory.
.B mdview README.md
.TP
View a README file located in another directory.
.B mdview /path/to/another/directory/README.md
.TP
View the existing index.md file in some directory; index.md is the HOMEPAGE.
.B mdview /path/to/some/directory
.TP
View an alternative index and make it the HOMEPAGE.
.B mdview /path/to/some/directory my_index.md
.TP
Search for "the" in the current directory, and view the results.
.B mdview search://the
.TP
Search for "the" in another directory, and view the results.
.B mdview /path/to/directory search://the
.TP
Convert a Markdown file to HTML.
.B mdview \-\-html README.md

.sp 1




[REPORTING BUGS]
Known bugs: <\fIhttps://github.com/step-/mdview/wiki/Known-bugs.md\fR>.

To report a new bug please open a ticket at <\fIhttps://github.com/step-/mdview/issues\fR>.
.LP
To troubleshoot Markdown syntax issues, try examining the output of the following command
in a browser:
.B mdview \-\-lint \-\-toc\-level=6 \-\-html \fBFILE\fR.



[SEE ALSO]
.LP
<\fIhttps://github.com/step-/mdview/wiki\fR>.
